      "player": "Opus Brewer",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Just a 1/1 Scion attacking. I could block with my Elf Warrior Token 1/1 to trade, but I'd lose a body for next turn's alpha strike. Actually, they're at 6 and I have 9 power across 4 creatures. Even losing the token (1 power), I'd have 8 power across 3 attackers and Titanic Growth for +4. More than enough.\n\
\n\
Let me trade the token to save 1 life — but actually, keeping more bodies is better because they have 4 blockers. If I have 4 attackers vs 4 blockers, they can block everything. If I only have 3 attackers, they still can block all 3. Hmm, the math:\n\
\n\
With 4 attackers (2+3+1+3 = 9), they block all 4 with their 4 creatures. I can Titanic Growth an attacker after blocks. If I pump whoever is blocked by a 1/1 Scion, the overflow goes through as... wait, none of my creatures have trample except I can't.\n\
\n\
Actually I need to think differently. They block all 4 of my creatures. Without trample, blocked creatures deal damage to blockers not to face. So I need unblocked creatures. If I have 4 attackers and they have 4 blockers, everything gets blocked and 0 damage gets through (without trample).\n\
\n\
So keeping the token doesn't help if they block everything. Better to just not block here, take 1, and then next turn I need to figure out how to get damage through.\n\
\n\
Wait — Herald has the Primeval Herald trigger. Let me re-check.",
