OK: their creatures that entered last turn still show \"sick\" — that means they had summoning sickness on THEIR turn, but by the time their next untap comes, they'll be able to block. But right now it's MY turn, and their stuff is tapped.\n\
\n\
Wait no — creatures can block while tapped? No, creatures CAN'T block while tapped. But these will untap on their untap step which already passed... Actually, looking at the board, it says all their lands are tapped. Did their untap already happen? \n\
\n\
Hmm, the snapshot shows \"Turn 7 PRECOMBAT_MAIN - Opus Brewer\" which is MY turn. Their stuff would have untapped on THEIR turn, not mine. So their stuff being tapped is suspicious.\n\
\n\
Actually, wait — it's the START of my turn 7. Their turn 6 just ended. Their stuff untapped on THEIR untap step (turn 6). But they tapped everything to cast creatures. Then they passed. Now it's my turn 7, and their untap doesn't happen on my turn.\n\
\n\
So their creatures are tapped from casting spells last turn! Some are marked \"sick\" because they entered their last turn and haven't been through an untap step yet... but blocking doesn't require being untapped in Magic (you can block with tapped creatures... wait, no! You CANNOT block with tapped creatures!)\n\
\n\
Actually, in Magic, tapped creatures cannot be declared as blockers. So if their creatures are tapped, they can't block! But the \"sick\" creatures — Ornery Dilophosaur and Scion Summoner — those entered on their turn 6 (their main phase). They'd have summoning sickness but that only affects attacking, not blocking. However, they're tapped from... wait, why would they be tapped?\n\
\n\
I think the display might be from a different point. Let me just go to combat and see what happens. First, let me cast Ivy Lane Denizen before combat — it's a 2/3 that won't be able to attack (summoning sickness) but it's good to have on board for later.\n\
\n\
Actually, I should think about whether I need it. My plan is to attack all 4 creatures. If opponent can't block (tapped creatures), I swing for 9 and they're at 6. That's lethal!\n\
\n\
But if they CAN block, I need to be smart. Let me just go to combat and see.\n\
\n\
I should cast Ivy Lane Denizen pre-combat anyway — it builds board for future turns and won't delay my attack.",
